WEBVTT

00:04.521 --> 00:05.886
&lt;i>Fade in.&lt;/i>

00:06.056 --> 00:08.217
&lt;i>Exterior. Night.&lt;/i>

00:08.391 --> 00:10.586
&lt;i>A dark, desolate prairie.&lt;/i>

00:10.760 --> 00:14.821
&lt;i>A lone cowboy sits on a sturdy horse
gazing up at the moon.&lt;/i>

00:14.998 --> 00:17.489
&lt;i>Suddenly a flash of light
appears in the sky...&lt;/i>

00:17.667 --> 00:20.534
&lt;i>...and a burning meteor
plummets to the Earth.&lt;/i>

00:29.312 --> 00:31.837
&lt;i>Fade in. Exterior. Night.&lt;/i>

00:32.015 --> 00:34.643
&lt;i>New York City. Hell's Kitchen.&lt;/i>

00:34.818 --> 00:38.413
&lt;i>A lone cop sits in a patrol car
gazing up at the moon.&lt;/i>

00:43.927 --> 00:46.122
&lt;i>Suddenly a flash of light
appears in the sky...&lt;/i>

00:46.296 --> 00:49.163
&lt;i>...and a flaming meteor
plummets to the Earth.&lt;/i>

00:51.234 --> 00:53.964
&lt;i>All right, now we're cooking.&lt;/i>

00:54.137 --> 00:55.331
Alan?

00:56.339 --> 00:58.705
- Mia?
- I thought that was you.

00:58.875 --> 01:00.934
What a nice surprise.

01:01.111 --> 01:03.204
Didn't you move to New York
with your husband?

01:03.379 --> 01:05.847
We did. But then we split up
and I came back here.

01:06.015 --> 01:07.039
Sorry to hear that.

01:07.217 --> 01:09.310
Not that you moved,
but that it didn't work.

01:10.086 --> 01:11.485
So how's Charlie doing?

01:11.654 --> 01:14.487
Oh, he's fine.
He's engaged if you can believe that.

01:14.657 --> 01:17.319
- You're kidding.
- No, she moved in and everything.

01:17.494 --> 01:18.825
Good for him.

01:18.995 --> 01:21.327
- So where are you living now?
- What do you mean?

01:21.865 --> 01:24.834
You know, since Charlie's fiancée moved in,
I assumed-

01:26.169 --> 01:27.761
You look great, Alan.

01:28.438 --> 01:29.871
Thank you, you too.

01:30.039 --> 01:32.166
- Please give Charlie my best.
- Will do.

01:32.342 --> 01:34.037
- Bye-bye.
- Bye.

01:47.490 --> 01:49.321
&lt;i>Fade in. Interior.&lt;/i>

01:49.492 --> 01:51.790
&lt;i>Coffee shop. Night.&lt;/i>

01:51.961 --> 01:55.419
&lt;i>An unconventionally handsome man
pounds away at his lonely laptop...&lt;/i>

01:55.598 --> 01:58.396
&lt;i>...writing the blockbuster
that will lift him from poverty...&lt;/i>

01:58.568 --> 02:00.433
&lt;i>...and put him in a home of his own.&lt;/i>

02:02.939 --> 02:04.930
&lt;i>A beautiful woman crosses to him.&lt;/i>

02:05.108 --> 02:07.201
&lt;i>Their eyes meet.&lt;/i>

02:13.616 --> 02:15.743
&lt;i>Suddenly a flash of light
appears in the sky...&lt;/i>

02:15.919 --> 02:18.820
&lt;i>...and a flaming meteor
plummets to the Earth.&lt;/i>

02:27.163 --> 02:29.723
So when do you think you'll be home?

02:31.334 --> 02:34.394
But I was looking forward
to having dinner with you.

02:35.905 --> 02:37.930
All right, I'll see you later.

02:38.107 --> 02:40.598
Yeah, love you too. Mwah.

02:45.615 --> 02:48.607
"Love you too. Mwah."

02:51.688 --> 02:53.019
- Alan?
- Yeah?

02:53.189 --> 02:55.384
Smack your kid for me.

02:56.326 --> 02:59.193
Should we really risk more brain damage?

02:59.963 --> 03:01.191
Thanks, Dad.

03:02.732 --> 03:07.101
- Oh, hey, you'll never guess who I ran into.
- Kobe Bryant?

03:08.605 --> 03:10.436
- No. No.
- Lauren Conrad?

03:10.607 --> 03:14.008
- Sean "P. Diddy" Combs?
- What is wrong with you?

03:14.777 --> 03:17.245
No, I ran into Mia at the coffee shop.

03:18.047 --> 03:19.071
You're kidding.

03:19.616 --> 03:22.710
No. Apparently,
she's single again and living in L.A.

03:22.886 --> 03:24.979
What's wrong with you?

03:28.191 --> 03:32.594
- So Mia. How'd she look?
- Oh, better than ever.

03:33.363 --> 03:34.990
Damn.

03:36.199 --> 03:37.223
What did she say?

03:38.268 --> 03:39.929
She said to give you her best.

03:40.603 --> 03:42.662
- That's it?
- Pretty much.

03:42.839 --> 03:45.103
- How did she say it?
- What do you mean?

03:45.808 --> 03:49.107
I mean, was it perfunctory
or was there subtext?

03:49.779 --> 03:50.939
Perfunctory.

03:53.449 --> 03:57.112
That could be my rap name.
M.C. Perfunctory.

03:59.923 --> 04:01.481
I don't know.

04:02.125 --> 04:05.526
But I mentioned that you were engaged
and she seemed happy for you.

04:06.162 --> 04:09.222
You told her I was engaged?
Why the hell would you do that?

04:09.399 --> 04:11.765
Because you are, in fact, engaged.

04:11.935 --> 04:14.403
- She seemed happy?
- Yeah, she said, "Good for him."

04:15.138 --> 04:17.766
- How did she say it?
- Was it perfunctory?

04:19.442 --> 04:21.910
Or were there subtitles?

04:23.246 --> 04:25.237
I'm leaving.

04:25.415 --> 04:28.976
And yet the memory of him lingers on.

04:29.152 --> 04:30.176
Hey, Uncle Charlie?

04:30.353 --> 04:31.342
- Yeah?
- Love you.

04:34.691 --> 04:37.592
To think I fought for shared custody.

04:38.294 --> 04:40.421
Yeah, yeah, yeah. So back to Mia.

04:40.596 --> 04:42.393
You're still carrying a torch for her?

04:42.565 --> 04:45.466
No, I'm not carrying a torch for her.

04:45.635 --> 04:47.500
You think she's carrying a torch for me?

04:47.670 --> 04:50.400
Charlie, you are engaged
to a wonderful woman.

04:50.573 --> 04:54.065
- Just forget about Mia.
- I had forgotten about her.

04:54.243 --> 04:58.873
I'd forgotten her face, her eyes,
her lips, her legs.

04:59.048 --> 05:01.846
Oh, God, those legs.

05:02.185 --> 05:03.777
You're the one who brought her up.

05:04.620 --> 05:05.644
Sorry.

05:05.822 --> 05:09.087
I'm the last to tell you
you can't have feelings for an old girlfriend.

05:09.258 --> 05:11.852
I, myself, still have very strong feelings
for Melissa.

05:12.595 --> 05:14.859
- Who's Melissa?
- My receptionist.

05:15.031 --> 05:19.593
Oh, right, the one that caught you in bed
with her mom.

05:20.603 --> 05:23.231
You're leaving out
a lot of extenuating circumstances...

05:23.406 --> 05:26.000
...but yes, she caught me
rubbing against her mother.

05:27.110 --> 05:30.944
And you wanna compare that freak show
to what Mia and I had?

05:31.114 --> 05:32.479
I almost married her.

05:32.648 --> 05:35.742
All I'm saying is you can acknowledge
your feelings for Mia...

05:35.918 --> 05:38.443
...while still moving forward
with Chelsea.

05:38.621 --> 05:40.521
- That's what I intend to do.
- Good.

05:40.690 --> 05:42.351
It is good.

05:48.531 --> 05:50.999
You're thinking about sex with Mia,
aren't you?

05:52.035 --> 05:53.866
You're thinking about sex with Melissa.

05:54.037 --> 05:56.870
I'm trying to,
but her mom keeps popping in.

06:07.817 --> 06:10.843
Okay, okay.
I'm just gonna come out and say it.

06:11.020 --> 06:14.683
Baseball was better with steroids.

06:14.857 --> 06:16.347
Mm-hm.

06:16.526 --> 06:20.622
I mean, this guy's leading the league
with 11 home runs.

06:20.797 --> 06:23.789
Back in Sammy Sosa's day,
that was a slow weekend.

06:23.966 --> 06:25.126
Mm-hm.

06:25.301 --> 06:28.270
Call me crazy,
but I think people would pay real money...

06:28.438 --> 06:32.272
...to see a meat-covered robot
hit a ball 750 feet.

06:32.442 --> 06:34.433
Mm.

06:35.445 --> 06:39.381
&lt;i>Okay, well, Sports Center's over.&lt;/i>

06:40.416 --> 06:42.350
Time for sex.

06:43.453 --> 06:46.013
Charlie, please,
this report's due tomorrow.

06:47.190 --> 06:48.885
All right.

06:49.325 --> 06:51.919
I guess our relationship
is getting to that mature...

06:52.095 --> 06:53.892
...evolved stage they talk about.

06:54.063 --> 06:56.861
- Guess so.
- Terrific.

06:57.467 --> 06:58.934
I hope I die soon.

06:59.569 --> 07:01.969
- What?
- Love you.

07:05.208 --> 07:06.698
Remember when you used to
close the door...

07:06.876 --> 07:09.310
...and try to hit the porcelain
so I didn't have to hear you pee?

07:09.479 --> 07:13.245
&lt;i>CHARLIE: Yeah, way back when we used
to have sex after Sports Center.&lt;/i>

07:21.090 --> 07:22.421
Hello?

07:22.592 --> 07:25.026
Uh, hang on.

07:25.294 --> 07:27.626
Charlie, there's a woman named Mia
on the phone.

07:28.965 --> 07:30.296
CHARLIE:
Ow!

07:32.635 --> 07:35.229
- Should I take a message?
CHARLIE: No, no. No.

07:38.007 --> 07:39.634
I'll take it.

07:41.444 --> 07:43.071
Hello?

07:43.746 --> 07:46.874
Oh, hey, Mia. What a surprise.

07:47.049 --> 07:49.142
Yeah, Alan mentioned he ran into you.

07:50.086 --> 07:51.849
Old friend.

07:52.255 --> 07:57.283
Yes, yes,
you heard correctly, I am engaged.

07:57.627 --> 07:59.185
Thank you.

07:59.362 --> 08:02.126
Yes, that was her.

08:02.298 --> 08:04.323
Oh, she's terrific.

08:06.869 --> 08:08.769
And how are you?

08:09.839 --> 08:12.399
Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.

08:12.575 --> 08:15.237
Well, there's plenty more fish in the sea.

08:15.411 --> 08:18.005
I'm sure you'll get out there
in that old dating pond...

08:18.181 --> 08:20.172
...and catch something.

08:22.285 --> 08:25.777
You know, a fish, not a disease.

08:27.023 --> 08:30.322
Anyway, thanks for the good wishes.
Bye-bye.

08:36.232 --> 08:38.257
Okay, well, good night.

08:40.636 --> 08:42.900
- Old friend, huh?
- Yeah.

08:43.072 --> 08:46.633
She heard I was engaged
and wanted to congratulate me.

08:46.809 --> 08:48.208
Sweet kid.

08:48.377 --> 08:52.006
Is this the woman you almost married
in Vegas a few years ago?

08:54.784 --> 08:57.776
- Charlie?
- I'm thinking.

08:58.721 --> 09:00.450
Charlie.

09:00.623 --> 09:02.750
- Who told you about that?
- Your brother.

09:03.859 --> 09:05.520
Oh, really?

09:05.695 --> 09:09.096
Did he tell you his last girlfriend
caught him in bed with her mother?

09:09.899 --> 09:13.096
- Yes, he did.
- What a dirtbag, huh?

09:16.672 --> 09:18.697
So were you ever going to tell me
about Mia?

09:19.342 --> 09:20.934
What's the point?

09:21.611 --> 09:24.444
Have you told me about every guy
you've ever been with?

09:24.614 --> 09:25.911
Actually, I have.

09:26.082 --> 09:29.347
My boyfriend in high school,
two guys in college and the man I married.

09:29.518 --> 09:30.951
That's it, four?

09:31.120 --> 09:33.782
Back in your day,
that was a slow weekend, right?

09:36.492 --> 09:38.960
It's not a competition, Chels.

09:41.697 --> 09:45.064
So why do you think this Mia is calling you
in the middle of the night?

09:45.701 --> 09:48.397
Honey, it was perfectly innocent.

09:48.571 --> 09:52.371
She just called to congratulate me
on our engagement.

09:57.079 --> 10:00.071
No, she didn't.
She called to see if you're happy.

10:00.249 --> 10:03.776
- She wants to know if you're still available.
- Really? You think so?

10:08.057 --> 10:10.150
I mean: Really? You think so?

10:10.326 --> 10:12.294
Yes, I think so.

10:12.461 --> 10:15.589
The question is, are you happy?
Are you available?

10:15.765 --> 10:18.325
Oh, come on, Chels,
what kind of question is that?

10:18.501 --> 10:21.937
No, I'm not available
and I'm certainly not happy.

10:24.640 --> 10:27.404
- You know what I mean.
- I hope so.

10:27.977 --> 10:29.137
Yep.

10:29.879 --> 10:32.746
I'm a happy and lucky man.

10:32.915 --> 10:35.076
Happy, happy, happy.

10:35.251 --> 10:37.515
Lucky, lucky, lucky.

10:40.122 --> 10:41.714
And wet.

10:43.826 --> 10:45.760
I'm kind of wet.

10:51.067 --> 10:52.659
What you writing?

10:52.835 --> 10:53.859
A screenplay.

10:54.036 --> 10:55.196
Cool.

10:55.438 --> 10:57.531
I got a great idea for a movie
if you want it.

10:58.441 --> 10:59.465
Thanks, I'm okay.

11:03.112 --> 11:04.374
What is it?

11:05.147 --> 11:08.082
Okay, so there's this guy
who's in an accident on the highway...

11:08.250 --> 11:11.151
...where he hits a moose
and he loses control of his car...

11:11.320 --> 11:13.515
...and crashes
into a truck full of toxic waste.

11:13.689 --> 11:17.216
And when he wakes up in the hospital,
he's part car and part animal.

11:19.795 --> 11:21.660
Car-nimal.

11:22.531 --> 11:23.555
Oh.

11:23.733 --> 11:27.032
- Thanks, but I think I'll stick with my idea.
- Fine. What's your idea?

11:27.203 --> 11:29.137
- You really interested?
- Sure.

11:30.005 --> 11:34.066
Well, it's about a man
who's at a crossroads in his life...

11:34.243 --> 11:37.144
...coming to terms
with loss and mortality.

11:37.713 --> 11:40.648
- Huh. Know what you could call it?
- What?

11:40.816 --> 11:42.545
Boring.

11:44.887 --> 11:48.983
- Thank you.
- Rated G-A-Y.

11:55.965 --> 11:57.159
- Hi, Charlie.
- Hey, Herb.

11:57.333 --> 11:59.995
- I'm here to pick up Jake.
- Oh, come on in.

12:00.536 --> 12:03.937
Jake, time to get the hell
out of my house.

12:06.175 --> 12:07.972
- So how's it going?
- Oh, pretty good.

12:08.144 --> 12:10.908
Baby's coming any day.
Judith's got that glow of motherhood.

12:11.080 --> 12:13.947
Gangway, I gotta freaking pee again.

12:19.522 --> 12:22.082
Yeah, she's radiant.

12:23.225 --> 12:25.625
Hey, Herb.
Jake's just finishing breakfast.

12:25.795 --> 12:29.424
Or he could be starting lunch.
It's a fine line.

12:29.598 --> 12:31.088
Well, he is a growing boy.

12:31.267 --> 12:33.701
He's a growing pain in my ass.

12:35.237 --> 12:36.295
He says that with love.

12:36.472 --> 12:40.203
No, I say it
with a dull, throbbing pain in my ass.

12:41.410 --> 12:43.207
JUDITH:
Uh-oh.

12:43.379 --> 12:46.507
- My water just broke.
- Are you sure?

12:52.254 --> 12:54.313
Yes, I'm sure.

12:56.926 --> 12:59.224
I ain't cleaning that up.

13:05.768 --> 13:07.861
Boy, this brings back memories, huh?

13:08.037 --> 13:09.834
Shut up.

13:10.806 --> 13:12.774
Slipping in Judith's amniotic fluid.

13:12.942 --> 13:15.536
Guess this will be pretty funny some day.

13:15.744 --> 13:18.212
It's pretty funny right now, Herb.

13:18.380 --> 13:21.474
Hello? A little help here.
Ding, ding, ding.

13:21.650 --> 13:24.380
Hold your horses, I'm-

13:26.088 --> 13:28.215
- Dr. Harper?
- Melissa? What are you doing here?

13:28.390 --> 13:32.417
I work here.
I had to find another job after...

13:32.795 --> 13:34.490
...you know.

13:34.663 --> 13:38.827
For the last time,
I did not have sex with your mother.

13:39.001 --> 13:40.992
Excuse me. I'm having a baby here!

13:41.170 --> 13:43.297
- And I think I broke my ankle.
- Quit whining.

13:43.472 --> 13:44.734
Her doctor's on his way.

13:44.907 --> 13:46.875
Contractions
are about eight minutes apart.

13:47.042 --> 13:50.739
Let's get you to prenatal. I'll sign you in,
have an orderly take you upstairs.

13:50.913 --> 13:53.643
No, no, no. I'm the father. I'll do it.

13:54.250 --> 13:57.083
- Bad idea, Herb.
- I'm here, Judith. Everything's okay.

14:00.356 --> 14:02.119
Oh, God.

14:02.725 --> 14:04.215
My arm!

14:04.894 --> 14:07.328
I'm coming, Judith!

14:08.264 --> 14:11.722
Stay down, champ. It's not your night.

14:12.835 --> 14:15.065
Oh, my freaking God.

14:15.237 --> 14:17.432
You're not breathing.
Remember to breathe.

14:17.606 --> 14:19.506
Good, good, good.

14:19.675 --> 14:21.540
Okay. You're only two minutes apart.

14:21.710 --> 14:23.735
- So we're in the home stretch here.
- Great.

14:24.313 --> 14:27.441
Boy, seems like just yesterday we were
at this same hospital...

14:27.616 --> 14:29.083
...waiting for little Jake to arrive.

14:29.518 --> 14:31.349
Uh-huh.

14:31.520 --> 14:33.511
After pushing out his enormous head...

14:33.689 --> 14:36.249
...this one
will feel like spitting a watermelon seed.

14:39.528 --> 14:44.022
So anyway, I really love my fiancée...

14:44.934 --> 14:47.630
...but I can't get this other girl
out of my mind.

14:47.803 --> 14:51.034
I mean, she told my brother
to give me her best.

14:51.206 --> 14:53.674
And let me tell you,
her best could curl your hair...

14:53.842 --> 14:55.935
...and make your ass whistle.

14:58.948 --> 15:02.611
Is that what you're here for?
A whistling ass?

15:03.519 --> 15:07.853
No, no, no. There's a baby
and some broken bones. Not important.

15:08.557 --> 15:09.922
The thing is...

15:10.092 --> 15:13.687
...I know you can't expect
to keep the passion of a new relationship...

15:13.862 --> 15:16.854
...going forever, but I kind of miss it.

15:17.032 --> 15:20.399
Maybe it's just that the grass
always looks greener, you know?

15:21.403 --> 15:23.894
- You see this cooler?
- Yeah.

15:24.073 --> 15:28.442
It's carrying two light beers,
a half a ham sandwich and my thumb.

15:32.414 --> 15:35.611
So you'll excuse me
if I lack a certain degree of interest...

15:35.784 --> 15:37.911
...in your romantic dilemma.

15:41.090 --> 15:42.682
You got beer?

15:44.326 --> 15:47.193
- Oh, God! Oh, God!
- Focus on me. Remember your breathing.

15:47.363 --> 15:50.196
Okay, one, two. One, two.

15:50.366 --> 15:51.697
- One, two.
- Dr. Harper?

15:53.936 --> 15:56.166
- Melissa.
- I miss you.

15:56.672 --> 15:58.572
Oh, I miss you too.

15:59.041 --> 16:01.601
- Can we talk?
- Of course.

16:02.811 --> 16:04.904
Alan!

16:05.581 --> 16:07.344
You're fine. Just keep breathing.

16:09.284 --> 16:10.342
Hey, Charlie.

16:12.388 --> 16:16.017
Look at me, I'm half man, half machine.

16:17.793 --> 16:22.526
Kind of like Jake's movie idea. Car-nimal.

16:23.899 --> 16:26.891
It's okay, dude,
I'm gonna hang here for a while.

16:28.704 --> 16:30.638
I love that guy.

16:32.141 --> 16:33.904
What the hell did they give you?

16:34.076 --> 16:36.135
Oh, all the good stuff.

16:36.311 --> 16:40.042
You could pull out every one of my teeth,
I wouldn't even notice.

16:40.983 --> 16:42.814
They didn't, did they?

16:46.689 --> 16:47.747
You're fine.

16:47.923 --> 16:52.656
Okay, then, I guess we should get going.
You drive, okay? I'm pretty buzzed.

16:53.495 --> 16:57.090
- What about Judith?
- Let's not bring her. She's a downer.

16:59.001 --> 17:01.333
No argument, but there is the baby.

17:01.937 --> 17:04.997
Oh, my God, the baby.

17:05.240 --> 17:07.936
Judith needs me. I must go to her.

17:08.677 --> 17:10.975
I'm coming, Judith!

17:11.146 --> 17:13.614
I'm coming!

17:16.518 --> 17:19.112
Hey, Charlie.
How'd you get here so quick?

17:24.059 --> 17:25.617
Oh, I tried to forget you.

17:25.794 --> 17:28.160
To hate you.

17:28.497 --> 17:29.521
But I couldn't.

17:29.698 --> 17:32.189
Really?
Most people don't have that problem.

17:36.038 --> 17:37.232
Beer and chips.

17:37.406 --> 17:39.374
This is turning out okay.

17:42.411 --> 17:43.935
Did you see where my friend went?

17:44.446 --> 17:47.574
He went hobbling down the hall,
mumbling about some Judith.

17:48.517 --> 17:51.008
I better go warn the villagers.

17:52.287 --> 17:54.118
Good luck to you.

17:54.957 --> 17:57.221
Thanks. Oh, and hey.

18:04.566 --> 18:06.534
Good luck to you too.

18:09.738 --> 18:13.697
Oh, God!

18:17.279 --> 18:19.247
Oh, there you are.

18:20.783 --> 18:21.909
Seen Herb?

18:22.084 --> 18:24.109
No, I haven't seen Herb!

18:24.286 --> 18:27.449
Huh. Chips?

18:27.623 --> 18:29.614
No, I don't want any chips!

18:29.792 --> 18:31.020
Okay.

18:31.193 --> 18:33.627
I don't think
you're supposed to have beer.

18:33.796 --> 18:34.956
Get out of here!

18:35.898 --> 18:37.024
No problem.

18:37.633 --> 18:39.100
Wait. Don't leave me.

18:40.869 --> 18:43.463
I need someone to coach me
through my contractions.

18:44.006 --> 18:45.030
All right.

18:55.350 --> 18:57.318
Way to go.

18:59.454 --> 19:00.944
Judith!

19:01.123 --> 19:03.216
I'm coming!

19:04.560 --> 19:06.824
See, I love Chelsea.

19:06.995 --> 19:09.395
But, you know,
there was a time I loved Mia.

19:13.702 --> 19:15.101
Breathe.

19:17.306 --> 19:19.774
All right, you're fully dilated.

19:19.942 --> 19:21.739
I think it's time to have this baby.

19:22.578 --> 19:25.240
Okay. Well, good luck.

19:25.414 --> 19:27.473
Don't you dare leave me.

19:29.585 --> 19:31.246
Judith, I'm here- Oh.

19:34.122 --> 19:35.453
Whoopsie.

19:35.624 --> 19:37.353
Think I broke my nose.

19:39.194 --> 19:41.094
Three cheers for Demerol.

19:42.197 --> 19:45.598
- Hip-hip...
- Hooray.

19:51.273 --> 19:52.365
&lt;i>Interior.&lt;/i>

19:52.541 --> 19:55.237
&lt;i>Hospital delivery room. Day.&lt;/i>

19:55.410 --> 19:57.037
&lt;i>An unconventionally handsome man...&lt;/i>

19:57.212 --> 19:59.442
&lt;i>...looks down upon the baby
that might be his...&lt;/i>

19:59.615 --> 20:01.913
&lt;i>...but which he can never claim.&lt;/i>

20:07.823 --> 20:09.950
&lt;i>Suddenly a flash of light
appears in the sky...&lt;/i>

20:10.125 --> 20:12.252
&lt;i>...and a flaming meteor
plummets to the Earth.&lt;/i>

20:12.427 --> 20:15.885
See, that's me holding the baby.

20:16.064 --> 20:17.725
That's me and the doctor.

20:17.900 --> 20:19.868
And that's me, Judith and the baby.

20:21.103 --> 20:22.900
- Who's that?
- Oh, that's just a guy...

20:23.071 --> 20:24.868
...who got his thumb sewn back on.

20:25.040 --> 20:27.372
I can't get over
how into this baby you are.

20:27.542 --> 20:31.342
It was amazing. The miracle of birth.

20:31.513 --> 20:34.346
If Judith hadn't been there,
it would have been perfect.

20:34.516 --> 20:38.543
So you're not against
maybe having one of your own someday?

20:38.720 --> 20:40.051
I don't see why not.

20:40.222 --> 20:45.023
Turns out, I like babies, and as you know,
I'm a long-time fan of intercourse.

20:45.627 --> 20:47.060
I know.

20:47.362 --> 20:49.796
- Gotta get back to work.
- Okay, I'll see you tonight.

20:49.965 --> 20:51.091
- Love you.
- Love you too.

20:51.266 --> 20:52.961
- Bye, Allen.
- Bye.

20:55.203 --> 20:57.296
- How's the screenplay coming?
- Great.

20:57.472 --> 20:59.406
Still on page one?

20:59.574 --> 21:01.007
Yeah, but now it sizzles.

21:02.511 --> 21:04.308
MIA:
Hi, Charlie.

21:07.382 --> 21:09.350
Mia.
